    'Dagger' => 'Dagger',
    'Dagger description' => 'The dagger is a simple weapon (as opposed to a martial weapon) with a multitude of properties. It is a finesse, light, range (20/60), and thrown weapon. In fact, it has more properties than any of the DnD 5e weapons, making it fantastically versatile, if a little underpowered. The dagger deals just 1d4 base damage with a successful hit, though of course a critical hit, class ability, or a magic dagger might modify this base damage.',
    'Dart' => 'Dart',
    'Dart description' => 'Darts in Dungeons and Dragons are a far cry from the little darts thrown at targets in bars. They’re most likely based on the Roman Plumbata, heavy weighted darts that were often tossed underhand up into the air to rain death and chaos down on enemy parties. These weapons had a barbed tip and metal shaft, along with a heavy lead weight, to make them fall with a good amount of force. The heavier metal shafts and weights were attached to a long wooden shaft with fletching to keep it moving straight once gravity took control. These were not little novelty playthings that you tossed gingerly, they could do some serious damage.',
    'Dice set' => 'Dice set',
    'Dice set description' => 'Dice were typically cubes carved from ivory, bone, wood, or even stone. And they were marked with numbers ranging from one to six. Though dice also came in a variety of other geometric shapes that sported more numbers. Typical dice sets came in leather cups, which were often used for rolling them, though others simply shook them in their hands before throwing them on to the floor or table. Multiple games could be played with dice, such as various gambling games and other bar-entertainment.',
    'Diplomats Pack' => 'Diplomats Pack',
